     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hello <span><span style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34)\"><span style=\"font-weight:normal\">Manuel,</span><br><span style=\"font-weight:normal\"><br>Sorry to intrude. I&#39;m a student with Márcio Basgalupp at São José dos Campos Brazil,<br>and I found you google group by luck.<br><br>I am reading the irace technical report and trying some first uses.<br>First, thanks for all the great work. I&#39;m learning a lot with your material.<br><br>Second, your code example using the irace for optimizing an SANN (Simulated Annealing algorithm) gives me an error,<br>it has something to do with the sapply function called at line 84 and 90. I&#39;m trying to fix it, but I could not find how.<br><br>You are passing a list as candidate and it gives an error of unused argument:<br><img src=\"https://groups.google.com/group/irace-package/attach/881f5bcf2fa28/Auto%20Generated%20Inline%20Image%201?part=0.1\" alt=\"\"><br><br>I&#39;ll keep trying to fix that and make it work.But as it&#39;s happening on your example code, I thought of telling you as fast as possible,<br>as other users might have the same difficulties.<br><br>Cheers.<br>Ricardo.</span><br></span></span></div>"
